Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:15:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] FK-16 (0.3.32 candidate 2): authority evaluation
 evidence, accurate readiness, one capability contract, gate fixes

Corrections from the final independent review of 0a35187:
- Hosted AuthBoundry keeps its documented contract (agent callers decided as the executor) and is now
  identified: authorityMode "hosted-executor-grants"; authority.local.agentCallers does not govern it.
- authorityMode (local-executor, local-per-agent, local-executor-grants-opt-in, hosted-executor,
  hosted-executor-grants) on every decision and in every durable record of it: activity (refusals FeltKit
  makes before asking AuthBoundry included), invocation decision notes, policy decision records,
  integration call records. Evidence only.
- Readiness authority.agent-callers never passes without knowing: hosted, not started, failed, no address,
  per-agent, refused, shared executor grants.
- authority.local: false/null/0/"" stay off (0.3.31); only configuration objects are validated.
- An agent caller refused for lack of per-agent delegation on a person's connection is FAILED_PRECONDITION
  ("retrying will not change this"), not UNAVAILABLE "try again".
- runtime/authority-contract.ts: one per-agent contract (registerAgent, revokeAgent, agentCredentialOf, agents
  on the started authority) used by the runtime, the tests and the release gate.
- release-prerequisites: capabilities probed by use (a private AuthBoundry started from the installed
  @authboundry/local + @authboundry/core: required); every installed upstream copy, nested ones included,
  compared with the registry tarball; metadata fetched online, tarball integrity checked; unpublished (E404)
  vs unreachable reported differently; offline refused; stderr passed through by release-check.
- Docs: POLICIES, CONNECTIONS, SECURITY, GUARANTEES, LOCAL-AUTHORITY, CHANGELOG agree.
- Tests: local default/opt-in, hosted, failed start, deferred start, falsy configuration, durable policy,
  invocation and integration evidence, retry guidance.

